└── README.md
```

## 🚀 How to Run the Project

### Using Google Colab

1. Open Google Colab.
2. Upload `Smart_campus_Energy_Analyzer.ipynb`.
3. Upload the Excel dataset when prompted.
4. Run all notebook cells in order.
5. Enter the required time value in the prediction section.
6. View the predicted electricity consumption.

### Install Required Libraries

```bash
pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn openpyxl
```

## 🔮 Sample Prediction

The notebook asks the user to enter a time value.

Example:

```text
Enter time in hours: 3

Time (Hours): 3
Predicted Electricity Consumption: Model Output kWh
```

*The predicted value depends on the trained model and dataset.*

